{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:00:46Z","content":"A copy of the BRD has been created, and **17 targeted review comments** have been added and anchored to the specific sections, requirements, and edge cases in the document:\n\n🔗 **[HR Agentic Solution BRD - Reviewed & Annotated](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MwYH70ssudg0-_SjPjZQndfjtsD0ca616YYNB0NgS5g/edit)**\n\n---\n\n### Summary of In-Line Comments & Architectural Feedback Added to the Doc\n\n| Location in Document | Anchor Text / Quote | Focus Area | Summary of In-line Comment |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Executive Summary** | `enforce traceably bounded execution, authenticate the automation's origin...` | **Architecture & Security** | Highlights the direct contradiction between zero-trust origin authentication and Section 6's exclusion of SSO/IdP. |\n| **Sec 1 (Objectives)** | `Reduce routine HR and IT helpdesk ticket volume by at least 40%...` | **Product Telemetry** | Requests baseline monthly Tier-1 ticket volumes and definitions for how \"deflection\" is measured (e.g., ticket avoided vs. session abandonment). |\n| **Sec 1 (Objectives)** | `Achieve zero policy violations and data leaks...` | **Risk & Feasibility** | Flags that \"zero policy violations\" is an unachievable deterministic guarantee with generative LLMs; recommends probabilistic benchmarks (`>99.5%`). |\n| **Sec 2.3 (Out of Scope)** | `Processing of payroll data, performance reviews, or compensation details.` | **Scope Contradiction** | Flags conflict with **UC-2.3** (quoting relocation allowances/limits) and expense policy guidelines. |\n| **Sec 3 (UC-1.2)** | `How many hours of PTO do I currently have accrued?` | **Data Model Ambiguity** | Points out contradiction between user prompt in \"hours\" vs. FR-3.2 balance constraints defined in \"work days\". |\n| **Sec 3 (UC-2.1)** | `order one for me?` | **UX & Safety Guardrail** | Recommends mandatory Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) confirmation before state mutations to prevent unintended autonomous ordering. |\n| **Sec 3 (UC-2.2)** | `Open ticket in ServiceImmediately to route user email access to manager.` | **SAGA / Consistency** | Flags high transaction risk if WorkWeek leave succeeds but ticket creation fails; demands automated compensating rollback / alert. |\n| **Sec 3 (UC-2.3)** | `get my building access sorted?` | **System Boundaries** | Inquires whether ServiceImmediately has an automated bridge to physical badging systems or is an unassigned ticket. |\n| **Sec 4.1 (FR-1.5)** | `The system must enforce strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)...` | **Security Blocker** | Asks how RBAC will be enforced when using shared test credentials without SSO; recommends signed mock-identity JWT headers. |\n| **Sec 4.3 (FR-3.2)** | `validating that the request does not exceed remaining accrued days.` | **Missing Functional Scope** | Flags missing Leave Cancellation, Modification, Approval Tracking, and company holiday/weekend calendar exclusion rules. |\n| **Sec 4.3 (FR-3.4)** | `No employee-specific dynamic data should be cached in the AI orchestration layer.` | **Performance & Resilience** | Identifies latency and outage risks during WorkWeek 503/429 events; recommends read-through circuit breaker patterns. |\n| **Sec 4.4 (FR-4.2)** | `Transition the lifecycle state of a ticket (e.g. to 'Resolved' or 'Closed')...` | **Permissions & Governance** | Recommends restricting end-users to 'Cancel' or 'Reopen', reserving 'Resolved'/'Closed' for technicians. |\n| **Sec 4.4 (FR-4.3)** | `Scan for potential duplicate tickets submitted in quick succession...` | **Underspecified Requirement** | Demands concrete parameters: deduplication time window, similarity threshold, and resolution behavior (block vs. prompt vs. append). |\n| **Sec 4.5 (FR-5.5)** | `within [X] hours/minutes of the document being updated in the source repository.` | **Missing SLA** | Highlights the unresolved `[X]` placeholder; recommends $\\le 1$ hr for automated webhooks or 24 hrs for daily batch sync. |\n| **Sec 5.2 (NFR-2.1)** | `The system must begin generating a response within 10 seconds...` | **Performance Target** | Identifies 10s TTFT as too slow for conversational UX (target $p50 < 2.0s$); requests explicit end-to-end budgets for chained workflows. |\n| **Sec 5.4 (NFR-4.3)** | `provide instructions for manual follow-up or attempt compensating actions...` | **Architecture Decision** | Eliminates ambiguity around \"or\"; demands both automated compensating API calls and high-priority dead-letter queue (DLQ) alerts. |\n| **Sec 6 (Constraints)** | `The system will use functional test credentials for backend integrations...` | **Critical Architecture Conflict** | Critical blocker: Using shared test credentials breaks RBAC and data isolation; recommends mock identity assertion layer in the chat gateway. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Strategic Recommendations for Engineering Kickoff\n\n1. **Resolve the Identity & Auth Architecture First:** Implement a signed mock-identity JWT header injected by the Chat UI to bind user sessions to `employee_id`, enabling RBAC testing even with backend service accounts.\n2. **Mandate User Confirmation Cards:** Transition from fully autonomous tool execution to a Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) model where all state-mutating actions (leave bookings, address updates, ticket submissions) require explicit user review and confirmation.\n3. **Partition Scope for MVP 1 (MoSCoW):** Focus MVP 1 strictly on single-system operations (Policy RAG, WorkWeek leave check/submit, ServiceImmediately status/create). Defer autonomous cross-system orchestration (UC-2.x) to Phase 2 to eliminate multi-system rollback/SAGA risks."}
